The country of Brazil occupies roughly half of [[South America]], bordering the [[Atlantic Ocean]]. Brazil covers a total area of {{convert|8514215|km2|abbr=on}} which includes {{convert|8456510|km2|abbr=on}} of land and {{convert|55455|km2|abbr=on}} of water. The highest point in Brazil is [[Pico da Neblina]] at {{convert|2994|m|abbr=on}}. Brazil is bordered by the countries of [[Argentina]], [[Bolivia]], [[Colombia]], [[Guyana]], [[Paraguay]], [[Peru]], [[Suriname]], [[Uruguay]], [[Venezuela]], and [[French Guiana]].

Much of the climate is tropical, with the south being relatively temperate. The largest river in Brazil, and the second longest in the world, is the [[Amazon River|Amazon]].

